 "subs": [
  {
   "text": "16.89 GB",
   "start": 16.163,
   "duration": 16.448,
   "x": -560,
   "y": -230,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "1,604 files",
   "start": 16.613,
   "duration": 15.998,
   "x": 560,
   "y": -230,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "1 scene",
   "start": 17.063,
   "duration": 15.548,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "3 developers",
   "start": 17.513,
   "duration": 15.098,
   "x": 560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "This demo is sixteen point nine gigabytes.\nThat's bigger than most finished games I own.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "duration": 5.087
  },
  {
   "text": "Seven hundred and seventy megabytes of it is a file they\nforgot to delete. And there are three people on this team.",
   "start": 5.337,
   "duration": 6.576
  },
  {
   "text": "Expedition: Into Darkness is a medieval extraction crawler. You go\ndown with a torch, you fill your bag, and you try to get back out.",
   "start": 15.763,
   "duration": 8.3
  },
  {
   "text": "Nine hundred and eleven reviews, sixty nine percent positive. Mixed,\nin Steam's words. And about a thousand people are in it right now.",
   "start": 24.313,
   "duration": 8.248
  },
  {
   "text": "The median reviewer had five hours on it. The top ten\npercent, thirty six. One of them, two hundred and thirteen.",
   "start": 32.811,
   "duration": 6.707
  },
  {
   "text": "So people are staying. The argument is about\neverything around the game, not the game.",
   "start": 39.768,
   "duration": 4.591
  },
  {
   "text": "Steam publishes a file list for every demo, so\nlet's go through what three people actually shipped.",
   "start": 44.609,
   "duration": 5.557
  },
  {
   "text": "It's Unity, and the code is C sharp — you can tell because the build has a\nGame Assembly D L L, which is what the I L two C P P compiler leaves behind.",
   "start": 50.416,
   "duration": 9.685
  },
  {
   "text": "That's C sharp translated into C plus plus and compiled\nnative. You write the easy language and ship the fast one.",
   "start": 60.351,
   "duration": 7.099
  },
  {
   "text": "Audio is F MOD Studio, with Google's\nResonance Audio next to it for spatial sound.",
   "start": 67.7,
   "duration": 5.087
  },
  {
   "text": "In a game where the thing about to kill you is behind you in the dark, that isn't\ndecoration. That's the one middleware I'd argue three people should pay for.",
   "start": 73.037,
   "duration": 8.901
  },
  {
   "text": "There's also a native plugin in there called R F Lib C Native. It shows up in other Unity\ngames and I could not work out what it does. If you know, the comments are right there.",
   "start": 82.188,
   "duration": 10.86
  },
  {
   "text": "Now the size, because\nthat's the story here.",
   "start": 93.298,
   "duration": 2.814
  },
  {
   "text": "One scene in the whole build. Twenty three kilobytes. Everything else\nstreams in from fifteen hundred and fifty five Addressable bundles.",
   "start": 96.362,
   "duration": 7.647
  },
  {
   "text": "Those bundles are fifteen and a half gigabytes.\nThe single biggest one is two gigabytes on its own.",
   "start": 104.259,
   "duration": 5.61
  },
  {
   "text": "Some of that is honest. Look at the crafting screen: every weapon is separate\nparts, a shaft and a head, each with its own durability and inertia.",
   "start": 110.119,
   "duration": 7.961
  },
  {
   "text": "That means a mesh and a texture set for every part, not every weapon.\nArmour is the same, piece by piece. Content adds up fast when it's modular.",
   "start": 118.33,
   "duration": 9.084
  },
  {
   "text": "But three people did not hand-model sixteen gigabytes of medieval kit. My\nguess is bought libraries and scanned assets, dropped in at source resolution.",
   "start": 127.664,
   "duration": 10.155
  },
  {
   "text": "And that's usually what a two gigabyte bundle means. Not too\nmuch art. Art that never got its compression settings looked at.",
   "start": 138.069,
   "duration": 6.707
  },
  {
   "text": "Then there's the file\nthat isn't art at all.",
   "start": 145.026,
   "duration": 3.05
  },
  {
   "text": "Game Assembly dot P D B. Seven hundred and forty\nfive megabytes of debug symbols, shipped to players.",
   "start": 148.326,
   "duration": 6.472
  },
  {
   "text": "Symbols are how you read a crash report. They belong on your build\nserver, not in the download. Nobody has ever needed them to play a game.",
   "start": 155.048,
   "duration": 8.013
  },
  {
   "text": "With the other four, that's seven hundred and\nseventy megabytes of a demo doing nothing.",
   "start": 163.311,
   "duration": 4.904
  },
  {
   "text": "And the store page says you need eight gigabytes\nof storage. The build is sixteen point nine.",
   "start": 168.465,
   "duration": 5.322
  },
  {
   "text": "None of this is incompetence. It's what happens when\nthere are three of you and nobody owns the build.",
   "start": 174.037,
   "duration": 5.322
  },
  {
   "text": "Which shows up in the reviews\nexactly where you'd expect.",
   "start": 179.609,
   "duration": 3.102
  },
  {
   "text": "Performance is the loudest complaint by a distance. Blurry,\npoorly optimised, and a volumetric fog you can't turn off.",
   "start": 182.961,
   "duration": 7.308
  },
  {
   "text": "Co-op, meanwhile, gets a hundred and six mentions in positive reviews and\neight in negative ones. Three people built five player netcode that works.",
   "start": 190.519,
   "duration": 8.614
  },
  {
   "text": "And people who recommended it had played seven\nand a half hours. People who didn't, one.",
   "start": 199.383,
   "duration": 5.845
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's the whole\nteardown on one card.",
   "start": 205.478,
   "duration": 2.214
  },
  {
   "text": "Unity, I L two C P P, so the code is C sharp. Three people. F MOD and Resonance for\naudio. And seven hundred and seventy megabytes of debug symbols nobody meant to ship.",
   "start": 207.942,
   "duration": 12.558
  },
  {
   "text": "Worth a dip, and it's free while\nthe early access date moves around.",
   "start": 220.75,
   "duration": 4.173
  },
  {
   "text": "If you're shipping this year, two checkboxes. Strip your symbols. Then\nopen your own store page and check the number you wrote for storage.",
   "start": 225.173,
   "duration": 7.517
  },
  {
   "text": "That's my read of it from the outside. If you made this and I got\nsomething wrong, say so in the comments and I'll pin the correction.",
   "start": 232.94,
   "duration": 6.524
  },
  {
   "text": "Next time, another demo, another\nfile list. This is Demo Dip.",
   "start": 239.714,
   "duration": 4.774
  }
 ],
